{
"As for Chin, what is there that will satisfy it?": "9f86dd4f7443",
"At night he was let down by a rope and went out. He saw the Earl of Ch'in and said:": "69cf91f9e5a9",
"Besides, you once did the ruler of Chin a favor. He promised you Chiao and Hsia — and crossed the river in the morning and by evening was building walls against you. You know this.": "457adfcec3c8",
"But if Cheng falls, it will not go well for you either.": "3b7f97c4e29b",
"But to cross another state in order to hold distant land as your frontier — you know how hard that is.": "bbb2d0e54ade",
"Ch'in and Chin are besieging Cheng; Cheng already knows that it is finished.": "d267dda9942d",
"Chu declined: When I was in my prime I was still no better than other men; now I am old and can do nothing.": "6bdfba2bee6f",
"Having made Cheng its eastern border, it will want to extend its western border too. If it does not cut into Ch'in, where else is it to take from?": "c106ab6bf11a",
"He agreed.": "9e497c5bdf65",
"I Chih-hu said to the Earl of Cheng: The state is in danger. If you send Chu Chih-wu to see the ruler of Ch'in, the armies will surely withdraw.": "8c87362c3af9",
"If instead you spare Cheng and make it your host on the eastern road, so that your envoys going and coming are supplied when they run short, you lose nothing by it.": "056fb57752e7",
"If the fall of Cheng would be of benefit to you, I would venture to trouble your officers with the matter.": "d7c1f2e9efac",
"Let us go home. And he too withdrew.": "92c0dd0cf08e",
"The Chin army camped at Han-ling, the Ch'in army south of the Fan.": "2cb18d019a86",
"The Earl of Ch'in was pleased. He made a covenant with the men of Cheng, left Ch'i-tzu, P'ang-sun and Yang-sun to garrison it, and went home.": "5c8f94b1b7b6",
"The Marquis of Chin and the Earl of Ch'in laid siege to Cheng, because Cheng had been discourteous to Chin and had also leaned toward Ch'u.": "8f9ddfc924de",
"The duke followed his advice.": "a3893b1faf1c",
"The duke said: No. Without that man's help I would never have come to this.": "c3cbe95091a5",
"The duke said: That I did not use you earlier, and now in an emergency come begging you — that is my own fault.": "2ad04d12d040",
"To cut into Ch'in in order to benefit Chin — I leave it to you to consider.": "1a4ab1706900",
"To exchange order for disorder is not soldierly.": "f76412142a5c",
"To lose one's ally is not wise.": "482bf905603d",
"To rely on another's strength and then injure him is not humane.": "08f52503c830",
"Tzu-fan asked leave to attack them.": "8c037401a553",
"What use is it to destroy Cheng in order to enlarge your neighbor? Your neighbor's gain is your loss.": "b741d6160b6d"
